<title>INDIA: Indian Shaving 96/97 net 51.5 mln rupees.</title>
<headline>Indian Shaving 96/97 net 51.5 mln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		  51.5  vs  36.6</p>
<p>    Div (rupees)		 1.75 vs   1.50</p>
<p>    Net sales		1,197.6  vs 833.0</p>
<p>    Other income		 14.0 vs  12.7</p>
<p>    Total expenditure	 999.0 vs 686.6</p>
<p>    Interest costs	     54.9 vs  41.7</p>
<p>    Depreciation		 90.5 vs  74.0</p>
<p>    Extraordinary items	 8.6 vs   6.8</p>
<p>    Tax			     7.1 vs   nil</p>
<p>NOTE: U.S.-based Gillette Co holds a majority stake in Indian Shaving Products Ltd (ISPL). ISPL said in a statment it made a provision for taxation following the imposition of a minimum alternate tax (MAT) on corporations. It did not explain the extraordinary items.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
